    "body": "No built-in subclass of HTMLElement, is what I meant.\r\n\r\nRe: question begging. In general custom elements are not meant to be arbitrarily powerful; they're meant to give you the same power as the platform has. Anything we allow beyond that leads to people building un-idiomatic \"custom elements\" which don't behave like other elements, and might be better suited for a non-custom-elements technology.",
